{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "SQL", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear or use to define and talk about SQL.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations.  Explain briefly how different programming languages work.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.   Describes common activities related to Software Programming through the use of appropriate expressions, grammar and vocabulary in written or spoken situations according to the abilities related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "stream processing ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the speed rate at which information is streamed", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: it's designed for organizing data in relational database management systems (RDBMS), also for stream processing in relational data stream management systems (RDSMS).", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "data insert ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a statement to add one or more records in a single table in a relational database", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Remember that these models allow programmers the use of specific SQL protocols for data insert.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "query ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to ask or inquire about something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When working with SQL there are also: query, schema creation and modification, and data access control.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "cutting-edge ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the leading position in any given field", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Cutting-edge technology works with this database language.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "statement", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in technology: an input order or phrase", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Are you used to working with SQL specific protocols and statements?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "bear", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to keep in mind, not to forget about something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's very important to bear in mind that learning the whole syntax of the language is hard work.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Do some further research on SQL. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Prepare a presentation including the new information you consider relevant. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create a presentation using slides to show your findings. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your findings with your class.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I get new information on SQL. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I design a presentation with relevant information. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my findings with the class.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Be Used to + Ing in Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use <strong>be used to + ing</strong> to talk about present habits. This means that you have certain routines in your life or habits you developed for some time now. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can also use it to ask a person for those actions that have become a habit in their lives. Let's see how it works.</br> </br> To talk about habits acquired in the present, you can use the following structure: </br> </br> <div class=\"center_text\">Subject + <b>verb to be</b> + <b>used to </b>+ <b>verb</b> + <b>ing</b> + complement </div>  Example: </br> <i>I'<b>m used to working</b> with JavaScript instead of working with SQL.</i> </br> </br> In order to make questions using this structure, you just have to place the <b>verb to be</b> at the beginning of the sentence, the way we do when asking questions with just <b>verb to be</b> (this, of course, when you are not asking a content or <b>Wh- question</b>, in that case, you need to place the <b>Wh-</b> before the <b>verb to be</b>). </br> </br> This is the structure: </br> </br>           <div class=\"center_text\"> (Wh-) + <b>verb to be</b> + subject + <b>used to</b> + <b>verb</b> + <b>ing</b> + complement</div> Examples: </br> <i><b>Are</b> you <b>used to working</b> with SQL? </i></br> <i>Why <b>are</b> you <b>used to working</b> with SQL instead of JavaScript? </i>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Are you used to taking advantage of the whole potential of a programming language?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Are you used to working with SQL specific protocols and statements?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Am I used to managing information with relational models?", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Common content words and expressions used in SQL.", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "The following is a glossary of words used when working with SQL. Let's see what they mean.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<strong>Stream:</strong> The speed at which you download or upload, or transmit information from one storage device to another.</br></br>    <strong>Processing:</strong> The ability and speed rate at which machines process information in a given language.</br></br>   <strong>Data definition language:</strong> A language in which you introduce data in a program. </br></br>   <strong>Schema creation:</strong> One of the functions of SQL with which the language can create a database scheme to manage information.</br></br>     <strong>Database language:</strong> SQL is a database language. This means that programmers developed SQL specifically to create databases and organize and manage large amounts of information.</br></br>   <strong>Relational model:</strong> It is a model that a certain language follows, such as SQL, in order to create a relational scheme through which manage database information.", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can explain what SQL is.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can describe how SQL works.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can identify and understand key features and concepts related to SQL.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "What do you know about computer programming languages?  ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What features do you consider are important in programming languages?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type"