g steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}], "type": "post_instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}], "type": "learning_skills"}], "id": 11, "type": "DWS"}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}], "type": "lab_options"}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "id": 3, "contents": [{"value": {"coverimg": "enpe7n4le03ob07re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"time": "0", "text": "SQL, which stands for Structured Query Language, is a special-purpose domain-specific programming language I'm used to working with because it's designed for organizing data in relational database management systems (RDBMS), also for stream processing in relational data stream management systems (RDSMS). This is to say that SQL is a data definition language for database language, which is a very useful tool in schema creation using a relational model. </br></br>I have to tell you, guys, cutting-edge technology works with this database language, this is why you have to ask yourself: as an engineer or programmer, am I used to managing information with relational models? Remember that these models allow programmers the use of specific SQL protocols for data insert, updating, and deleting such data.</br></br>", "image": "enpe7n4le03ob07re2img01.jpg", "id": 0}, {"time": "63000", "text": "Remember that data security is one of the most important aspects for companies nowadays. This is why languages such as SQL became so popular since the 70's because you can use them in order to manage large amounts of information in a very intuitive and efficient way. As a very well trained programmer, are you used to working with SQL specific protocols and statements? If so, streaming information using scheme creation by means of a relational model, which is one of the most outstanding characteristics SQL provides the programmer with, is going to be just what you want to specialize in. </br></br>", "image": "enpe7n4le03ob07re2img02.jpg", "id": 1}, {"time": "107000", "text": "Are you used to taking advantage of the whole potential of a programming language? When working with SQL there are also: query, schema creation and modification, and data access control, which I'm used to putting to the test in my current job. Now, things are not that easy with SQL. It's very important to bear in mind that learning the whole syntax of the language is hard work.", "image": "enpe7n4le03ob07re2img03.jpg", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe7n4le03ob07re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}]}